  "result": "Done! I've added VAT (Value Added Tax) calculation to the invoicing system:\n\n**VAT Calculation:**\n- Calculated per line on the amount AFTER discount: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n- Each line's VAT rounded using `roundCents()`\n- Invoice's total VAT is the sum of rounded line VATs (never a percentage of invoice total)\n\n**Updated `invoiceTotals`:**\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n- All amounts clamped to \u2265 0\n\n**Updated `renderInvoiceText`:**\n- Shows VAT line just above Total (only if VAT > 0)\n- Format: `VAT: \u20acxyz.xx`\n\n**Updated and added tests:**\n- Fixed 12 existing tests to account for VAT in totals\n- Added 8 comprehensive new tests covering:\n  - VAT with different rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n  - VAT calculated after discount\n  - Mixed VAT rates\n  - Decimal rounding\n\nAll 106 tests pass \u2713",
